1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,030
Choosing a document scanning company in Singapore?

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:11,930
A wrong choice often shows up months later, as a PDPA gap, a retention mismatch, or an archive with no backup.

3
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,790
Here is what to check.

4
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:25,300
First, match the vendor to your formats: office documents with OCR, large-format drawings, bound books and ledgers, or microfilm and microfiche, which need specialised equipment.

5
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:30,590
Ask for written chain-of-custody from collection to return or certified destruction.

6
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:38,120
Check where files are processed and stored, and whether the vendor knows the five-year retention rules for accounting records.

7
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:42,270
For public-sector work, look for GeBIZ registration.

8
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:51,600
On the first call, ask who handles your originals, and what the end deliverable is: indexing, OCR, or a hybrid microfilm backup.

9
00:00:52,100 --> 00:01:02,760
Hybrid archiving keeps the digital layer for access and adds microfilm, rated LE-500 to ISO 18901, as an offline copy that ransomware cannot encrypt or alter.

10
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:11,380
Micrographics Data, in Singapore since 1989, assesses volume and condition on site or from samples before quoting.

11
00:01:11,730 --> 00:01:14,940
Request a quote at micrographicsdata.com.
